2026-09-27T09:27:27.3852616Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3852713Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3852854Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3852989Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3853035Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3853138Z ================
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3853199Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3853276Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3853478Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3853582Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3853638Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3905180Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3905355Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3905461Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3905777Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3906042Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3906609Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3907080Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3907182Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3907614Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3908004Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3908205Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3908424Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3908717Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3908788Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3908936Z ========
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3909019Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3909921Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3910966Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3911162Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3911525Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3912277Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3912750Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3913198Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3913553Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3913888Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3913979Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3914181Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3914303Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3915164Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3916132Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3916651Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3917364Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:27:27.3917722Z 
